1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,064
In this lesson, you'll make your
booking calendar work harder.

2
00:00:04,064 --> 00:00:08,261
We'll collect the right details when
people book, take a deposit by card,

3
00:00:08,261 --> 00:00:11,537
and make sure everyone gets
a confirmation straight away.

4
00:00:12,396 --> 00:00:15,070
We'll set up Bloom's implant consultation,

5
00:00:15,070 --> 00:00:18,253
a longer appointment where
a no-show really hurts.

6
00:00:18,253 --> 00:00:22,646
Open it from Calendar Settings, then
go to the Forms and Payment tab.

7
00:00:22,646 --> 00:00:25,638
The same steps work on
any calendar you create.

8
00:00:26,489 --> 00:00:31,495
By default, the booking form asks for
four things: first name, last name,

9
00:00:31,495 --> 00:00:32,592
phone and email.

10
00:00:32,592 --> 00:00:35,884
That's enough to create
the contact in your CRM,

11
00:00:35,884 --> 00:00:38,627
and to send confirmations and reminders.

12
00:00:39,477 --> 00:00:41,416
For new patients, we need more.

13
00:00:41,416 --> 00:00:45,170
Choose Custom form, and select
a form you've built in Sites,

14
00:00:45,170 --> 00:00:47,046
like New Patient Registration.

15
00:00:47,046 --> 00:00:52,176
Now patients give their date of birth,
current dentist and any medical notes while

16
00:00:52,176 --> 00:00:52,801
they book.

17
00:00:53,651 --> 00:00:57,806
The form also asks for consent
to text and email reminders.

18
00:00:57,806 --> 00:01:03,089
You'll want that in place before you
switch on the reminders in lesson 5.6.

19
00:01:03,940 --> 00:01:04,858
Next, payments.

20
00:01:04,858 --> 00:01:06,448
Switch on Accept payments.

21
00:01:06,448 --> 00:01:10,241
Kyntlo charges the card through
your connected Stripe account,

22
00:01:10,241 --> 00:01:12,933
so the money goes
straight to your business.

23
00:01:12,933 --> 00:01:17,521
If Stripe isn't connected yet, you'll
do that under Payments, in Module 12.

24
00:01:18,371 --> 00:01:19,478
Enter the amount.

25
00:01:19,478 --> 00:01:23,581
Bloom takes a £50 deposit, which
comes off the treatment later.

26
00:01:23,581 --> 00:01:28,987
Deposits cut no-shows dramatically, because
people turn up for appointments they've

27
00:01:28,987 --> 00:01:30,094
already paid for.

28
00:01:30,944 --> 00:01:32,398
Add a short description.

29
00:01:32,398 --> 00:01:37,064
It appears on the patient's receipt, so
they know exactly what they paid for,

30
00:01:37,064 --> 00:01:39,669
and that it counts
towards their treatment.

31
00:01:39,669 --> 00:01:44,395
Every payment is also recorded against
the contact, and listed under Payments,

32
00:01:44,395 --> 00:01:45,971
so your records stay tidy.

33
00:01:46,820 --> 00:01:51,328
Under After booking, choose what people
see once they've booked: a thank-you

34
00:01:51,328 --> 00:01:54,235
message, or a redirect to
a page on your website,

35
00:01:54,235 --> 00:01:57,735
for example one that explains
how to prepare for the visit.

36
00:01:58,586 --> 00:02:03,188
Confirmations live in the next tab,
Notifications and Additional Options.

37
00:02:03,188 --> 00:02:08,041
The booking confirmation goes out by
email and text the moment someone books,

38
00:02:08,041 --> 00:02:11,445
to the patient, and to the
team member they're seeing.

39
00:02:12,294 --> 00:02:16,917
Further down, Auto-confirm marks new
bookings as Confirmed straight away.

40
00:02:16,917 --> 00:02:21,033
Switch it off if you'd rather
review each booking yourself first.

41
00:02:21,033 --> 00:02:24,009
With a deposit taken,
auto-confirm makes sense,

42
00:02:24,009 --> 00:02:26,668
because the patient has already committed.

43
00:02:26,668 --> 00:02:27,682
Then click Save.

44
00:02:28,530 --> 00:02:29,428
Now preview it.

45
00:02:29,428 --> 00:02:33,441
Pick a time, and you'll see the
longer form, then the card payment,

46
00:02:33,441 --> 00:02:36,195
secured by Stripe, before
the booking is made.

47
00:02:36,195 --> 00:02:38,770
That's exactly what
your patients will see.

48
00:02:39,620 --> 00:02:40,742
Here's a pro tip.

49
00:02:40,742 --> 00:02:42,392
Keep booking forms short.

50
00:02:42,392 --> 00:02:45,163
Every extra question loses a few bookings.

51
00:02:45,163 --> 00:02:48,199
Ask only what you truly
need before the visit,

52
00:02:48,199 --> 00:02:51,234
and collect the rest
when the patient arrives.

53
00:02:52,188 --> 00:02:55,122
Your calendar now collects
details and deposits!

54
00:02:55,122 --> 00:03:00,257
Next, we'll connect your Google or Outlook
calendar, so you never get double-booked.

55
00:03:00,257 --> 00:03:01,113
See you there.
